        "name": "Injection",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The term is passed only as a bound parameter with %, _ and backslash escaped under an ESCAPE clause and nothing interpolated into the SQL; the surrounding wildcards are concatenated in constant SQL ('%' || ? || '%') rather than placed in the bound value, which is equally safe but not the exact form the rubric names."
